butors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pilot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c5ae1c7f9b6d4b899e","definition":"A person who is in charge of the controls of an aircraft.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["airman","airperson"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pilot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:90cc5d301935fb8cca","definition":"A sample episode of a proposed TV series produced to decide if it should be made or not. If approved, typically the first episode of an actual TV series.","example":"I think her biggest deal was she starred in a pilot.[…]Well, the way they pick TV shows is they make one show. That show's called a pilot. Then they show that one show to the people who pick shows, and on the strength of that one show, they decide if they wanna make more shows.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pilot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8d29b72e90033f30bd","definition":"A cowcatcher.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pilot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b594434944afe4a849","definition":"A racing driver.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Europe","register":"Europe","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pilot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-