ource":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pilot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:05a7be7aa7344a05d4","definition":"Being a vehicle to warn other road users of the presence of an oversize vehicle or combination.","example":"a pilot vehicle","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pilot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d461f42d71d0b5f848","definition":"To control (an aircraft or watercraft).","example":"I have visited more than half a dozen carrier training facilities, spent over 150 hours on jumpseats, piloted a Lockheed 1011 from MIA to LAX, visited numerous towers, rapcons, and centers, and discussed our commercial Air Transport System with everyone involved.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["aviate"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["pilotability","pilotable","repilot"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pilot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:84bd5aee21fb862487","definition":"To guide (a vessel) through coastal waters.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["pilotability","pilotable","repilot"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pilot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:62eac8f550406ea8d6","definition":"To test or have a preliminary trial of (an idea, a new product, television show, etc.)","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["pilotability","pilotable","repilot"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pilot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:82cadff63c9812ffbb","definition":"To serve as the leading locomotive on a double-headed train.","example":"One of the Midland Lines' Birmingham R.C.W. Type 2 diesels, No. D5403, made the debut of its class in the Manchester area on July 28 when it appeared in the early hours on freight; after four days in the area it left for the south piloting B.R./Sulzer Type 4 diesel No. D88 on the 2.25 Manchester Central-St. Pancras.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["pilotability","pilotable","repilot"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pilot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:05df519113f47723ac","definition":"To guide or conduct (a person) somewhere.","example":"Thus it came about that, three days later, I descended from the train at Styles St. Mary, an absurd little station, with no apparent reason for existence, perched up in the midst of green fields and country lanes. John Cavendish was waiting on the platform, and piloted me out to the car.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["pilotability","pilotable","repilot"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pilot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:22d34a47c38230d2cd","definition":"Acronym of payment in lieu of taxes","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"abbreviation, acronym, alt-of","register":"abbreviation, acronym, alt-of","wordFamily":["pilotability","pilotable","repilot"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/PILOT#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈpaɪ̯.lət/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/fb/En-us-pilot.ogg/En-us-pilot.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["pilotability","pilotable","repilot"]}